Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||10-16-2001||09:37 AM||||The above kit is the "Aldino" Which is based on the Ferrari 512BB. At last check their website was offline.  <A HREF="http://www.sit.wisc.edu/~ahbucha/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sit.wisc.edu/~ahbucha/</A> <P>Typically Testarossa Kits require a 7 inch stretch (check on ebay right now... there is a partially completed one in AZ for cheap).  A F355 kit typically requires a 3" frame stretch.<P>Check these places for more info/cars:<BR> <A HREF="http://priceofhistoys.com/showroom/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://priceofhistoys.com/showroom/index.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.paulsexotics.com/showroom.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paulsexotics.com/showroom.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.ck3.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ck3.com/</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://home1.gte.net/mpapich/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home1.gte.net/mpapich/index.htm</A> <P>...These are just a handful of links that I've found recently.  Also watch Ebay and Kitcars.com for kits in various stages of completion.  Good Luck!||||reg||1
